_progress\":\"not_measured\"},\"query\":\"Man Booker International Prize Wikipedia\",\"view\":\"full\"}]}","role":"tool","tool_call_id":"call_df06bf4730444385bcbfb97e"},{"content":"I have a strong lead from e1: Chigozie Obioma, born in Akure, Nigeria, whose novels \"The Fishermen (2015)\" and \"An Orchestra of Minorities (2019)\" were shortlisted for the Booker Prize and translated into 30 languages. Let me verify the puzzle structure. The award \"created in the 2000s\" = International Booker Prize (est. 2005). Now I need to confirm the connection: in the year one of Obioma's books was published (2015 or 2019), another book won the International Booker Prize that had been released the preceding year.\n\nLet me check the International Booker Prize winners and confirm the connection.","role":"assistant","tool_calls":[{"function":{"arguments":"{\"queries\": [\"International Booker Prize 2016 winner The Vegetarian Han Kang published 2015\", \"International Booker Prize 2019 winner Celestial Bodies published 2018\", \"Chigozie Obioma An Orchestra of Minorities International Booker Prize shortlist 2019\"], \"top_k\": 8}","name":"search"},"id":"call_b1c50c6c55414b50be00d9b8","index":0,"type":"function"}]},{"content":"{\"action_slot_charged\":true,\"executed\":true,\"ok\":true,\"results\":[{\"cached\":false,\"hits\":[{\"kind\":\"navigation_not_evidence\",\"navigation_seen\":true,\"previously_received\":true,\"raw_ranges_delivered\":[],\"read_action\":{\"ref\":\"d54\"},\"ref\":\"d54\",\"snippet\":\" ... Her best known novel, The Vegetarian (published in Korea in 2007), was her first to be translated into English, in 2015. It won the Man Booker International Prize in 2016, with the prize split between Han Kang and her translator, Deborah Smith.\\n\\nAt the time, Smith's translation ... \",\"title\":\"https://theconversation.com/my-novels-explore-human-suffering-nobel-prize-winner-han-kang-writes-with-empathy-for-vulnerable-lives-241064\"},{\"kind\":\"navigation_not_evidence\",\"navigation_seen\":true,\"previously_received\":true,\"raw_ranges_delivered\":[],\"read_action\":{\"ref\":\"d53\"},\"ref\":\"d53\",\"snippet\":\" ... literature winner Han Kang was eligible for this year's prize with her book We Do Not Part, translated from Korean by e. yaewon and Paige Aniyah Morris, she did not make the list. Kang won the International Booker in 2016 with her breakthrough novel, The Vegetarian, translated ... \",\"title\":\"https://www.theguardian.com/books/2025/feb/25/all-13-writers-on-international-booker-longlist-are-first-time-nominees\"},{\"kind\":\"navigation_not_evidence\",\"navigation_seen\":true,\"previously_received\":true,\"raw_ranges_delivered\":[],\"read_action\":{\"ref\":\"d55\"},\"ref\":\"d55\",\"snippet\":\" ... the International Booker prize in 2016—The White Book, Human Acts, and Greek Lessons. Kang, 53, has been a writer for over 30 years, but The Vegetarian was her first novel to be translated into English in 2015, and led to widespread acclaim and attention.\\n\\n\\\"Han Kang writes ... \",\"title\":\"https://time.com/7065011/nobel-prize-2024-winners/\"},{\"kind\":\"navigation_not_evidence\",\"navigation_seen\":true,\"previously_received\":true,\"raw_ranges_delivered\":[],\"read_action\":{\"ref\":\"d57\"},\"ref\":\"d57\",\"snippet\":\" ... Han is the author of five books that have appeared in English: The Vegetarian (2016, trans by Deborah Smith, Portobello)—which won the International Booker Prize, Human Acts (2017, trans by Deborah Smith, Portobello), The White Book (2018, trans by Deborah Smith, Portobello), Europa (2019, trans by Deborah ... \",\"title\":\"https://www.booksandpublishing.com.au/articles/2024/10/14/260359/han-kang-wins-2024-nobel-prize-for-literature/\"},{\"kind\":\"navigation_not_evidence\",\"navigation_seen\":true,\"previously_received\":true,\"raw_ranges_delivered\":[],\"read_action\":{\"ref\":\"d29\"},\"ref\":\"d29\",\"snippet\":\" ... the translator who won the 2016 Man Booker International Prize for her translation of The Vegetarian by Korean author Han Kang\\n\\nIt's of particular importance to note that the winning International Booker Prize comes from an independent press.\\n\\nIn a news conference earlier today, International Booker Prize ... \",\"title\":\"https://publishingperspectives.com/2022/05/geetanjali-shree-and-daisy-rockwell-win-the-international-booker-prize/\"},{\"kind\":\"navigation_not_evidence\",\"navigation_seen\":true,\"previously_received\":true,\"raw_ranges_delivered\":[],\"read_action\":{\"ref\":\"d34\"},\"ref\":\"d34\",\"snippet\":\" ... The Accusation, which was written in secret and smuggled out of the country, is his only published book to date. Deborah Smith is the Man Booker International Prize–winning translator of The Vegetarian by Han Kang and other books.\\n\\nHarmless Like You by Rowan Hisayo Buchanan\\n\\nRowan Hisayo ... \",\"title\":\"https://www.aspeninstitute.org/blog-posts/20-new-works-fiction-social-impact/\"},{\"kind\":\"navigation_not_evidence\",\"navigation_seen\":true,\"previously_received\":true,\"raw_ranges_delivered\":[],\"read_action\":{\"ref\":\"d56\"},\"ref\":\"d56\",\"snippet\":\" ... Deborah Smith, Korean to English: 'Han Kang is very generous… she calls them \\\"our\\\" books'\\n\\nDeborah Smith is translator of The Vegetarian by the Korean writer Han Kang; she and Kang are the co-winners of the Man Booker International prize 2016. She is also the translator of ... \",\"title\":\"https://www.theguardian.com/books/2016/jul/24/subtle-art-of-translating-foreign-fiction-ferrante-knausgaard\"},{\"kind\":\"navigation_not_evidence\",\"navigation_seen\":true,\"previously_received\":true,\"raw_ranges_delivered\":[],\"read_action\":{\"ref\":\"d59\"},\"ref\":\"d59\",\"snippet\":\" ... the names to watch out for?\\n\\nUndoubtedly the International Booker prize itself has boosted the profile of fiction from around the world published in English. Fiammetta Rocco has been the prize's administrator from its launch as an annual award in 2016, and since then its winners have ... \",\"title\":\"https://www.theguardian.com/books/2023/jul/29/its-exciting-its-powerful-how-translated-fiction-captured-a-new-generation-of-readers\"}],\"next_step\":\"Inspect navigation; read a relevant page or change the locating clue.\",\"observation\":{\"first_delivered_source_round\":null,\"prior_deliveries\":0,\"query_key\":\"cfdc86ac2a497f63621086096a8c4bcef37e10adb8aeaac5dd60c80fea02f83a\",\"replay_requested\":false,\"result_fingerprint\":\"52b8cb276e9e89ac3af3f1415e7997e08e731d892d47bf7a6ee853a79c4c2d1b\",\"semantic_progress\":\"not_measured\"},\"query\":\"International Booker Prize 2016 winner The Vegetarian Han Kang published 2015\",\"view\":\"full\"},{\"cached\":false,\"hits\":[{\"kind\":\"navigation_not_evidence\",\"navigation_seen\":false,\"previously_received\":false,\"raw_ranges_delivered\":[],\"read_action\":{\"ref\":\"d79\"},\"ref\":\"d79\",\"snippet\":\" ... Celestial Bodies: A Novel, Jokha Alharthi (Oct. 15)\\n\\nThree Omani sisters grapple with love and loss as their country quickly transforms due to the rise of the oil industry. Celestial Bodies, the first novel originally published in Arabic to win the Man Booker International Prize, showcases Oman's ... \",\"title\":\"https://time.com/5661400/best-books-fall-2019/\"},{\"kind\":\"navigation_not_evidence\",\"navigation_seen\":true,\"previously_received\":true,\"raw_ranges_delivered\":[{\"end\":6000,\"ref\":\"e2\",\"start\":0}],\"read_action\":{\"ref\":\"d5\"},\"ref\":\"d5\",\"snippet\":\" ... Man Booker Prize (2002–2019), is a prestigious literary award conferred each year for the best single work of sustained fiction written in the English language, which was published in the United Kingdom or Ireland. The winner of the Booker Prize receives , as well as international publicity that ... \",\"title\":\"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Booker_Prize\"},{\"kind\":\"navigation_not_evidence\",\"navigation_seen\":true,\"previously_received\":true,\"raw_ranges_delivered\":[{\"end\":3000,\"ref\":\"e1\",\"start\":0}],\"read_action\":{\"ref\":\"d30\"},\"ref\":\"d30\",\"snippet\":\" ... numerous prizes for fiction and non-fiction, and is the administrator of the International Booker Prize. Of Franco-Italian origin, she grew up in Kenya and read Arabic at Oxford University. Her book, The Miraculous Fever Tree, about malaria and the discovery of quinine, was published in Britain ... \",\"title\":\"https://www.oxbelly.com/fiction-writers-program/advisors\"},{\"kind\":\"navigation_not_evidence\",\"navigation_seen\":true,\"previously_received\":true,\"raw_ranges_delivered\":[],\"read_action\":{\"ref\":\"d25\"},\"ref\":\"d25\",\"snippet\":\" ... prize's fortieth anniversary, for \\\"The Best of the Booker\\\". In 2018 a special \\\"Golden Booker\\\" was awarded celebrating 50 years of the award; this was won by Michael Ondaatje for The English Patient.\\n\\nWinners, shortlists and longlists\\n\\n**Table 1**\\n\\n| Year | Award | Author | Title | Publisher | Judges |\\n|---|---|---|---|---|---|\\n| 1969 | Winner ... \",\"title\":\"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/List_of_winners_and_nominated_authors_of_the_Booker_Prize\"},{\"kind\":\"navigation_not_evidence\",\"navigation_seen\":false,\"previously_received\":false,\"raw_ranges_delivered\":[],\"read_action\":{\"ref\":\"d80\"},\"ref\":\"d80\",\"snippet\":\" ... 2022-02-20\\n---\\nThe Booker in the 2010s\\n\\n2010-19: New Frontiers\\n\\nThe 2010s were a hugely significant decade for the Booker, largely due to the shift in rules which came into place in 2014. From that year onwards, the Prize was open to all novels published in ... \",\"title\":\"https://www.ontheprize.co.uk/blog/the-booker-prize-in-the-2010s\"},{\"kind\":\"navigation_not_evidence\",\"navigation_seen\":true,\"previously_received\":true,\"raw_ranges_delivered\":[],\"read_action\":{\"ref\":\"d50\"},\"ref\":\"d50\",\"snippet\":\" ... Stories 2019 (Salt), short story 'Cluster'\\n\\nInvited judge for Reflex Flash Fiction Award\\n\\n2018: Named a Guardian Fresh Voice: Writers to Read Now\\n\\nShortlisted for the Not the Booker Award for Sealed\\n\\nLonglisted for the Sunday Times EFG Short Story Award and Galley Beggars Short Story Prize for ... \",\"title\":\"https://www.durham.ac.uk/staff/naomi-r-booth/\"},{\"kind\":\"navigation_not_evidence\",\"navigation_seen\":true,\"previously_received\":true,\"raw_ranges_delivered\":[],\"read_action\":{\"ref\":\"d6\"},\"ref\":\"d6\",\"snippet\":\" ... The book was the joint winner of the 2019 Booker Prize.\\n\\nNonfiction\\n\\nIn 2008, Atwood published Payback: Debt and the Shadow Side of Wealth, a collection of five lectures delivered as part of the Massey Lectures from October 12 to November 1, 2008. The book was released in ... \",\"title\":\"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Margaret_Atwood\"},{\"kind\":\"navigation_not_evidence\",\"navigation_seen\":true,\"previously_received\":true,\"raw_ranges_delivered\":[],\"read_action\":{\"ref\":\"d27\"},\"ref\":\"d27\",\"snippet\":\" ... Alice Munro has published 16 collections over her illustrious career. Her work has won the Nobel Prize in Literature, two Scotiabank Giller Prizes, three Governor General's Literary Awards and the Man Booker International Prize. Her first book, Dance of the Happy Shades, was released in 1968, and ... \",\"title\":\"https://www.cbc.ca/books/30-books-to-celebrate-30-years-of-writers-company-1.5755144\"}],\"next_step\":\"Inspect navigation; read a relevant page or change the locating clue.\",\"observation\":{\"first_delivered_source_round\":null,\"prior_deliveries\":0,\"query_key\":\"589da0a18f00f20eb91307760fb16da25a0a4609fb05a7be5a341ead1c92ac71\",\"replay_requested\":false,\"result_fingerprint\":\"3b43ad34fab235434fa0197c0acdf29ce5b1404f9e5ce152971f48d104c3c46f\",\"semantic_progress\":\"not_measured\"},\"query\":\"International Booker Prize 2019 winner Celestial Bodies published 2018\",\"view\":\"full\"},{\"cached\":false,\"hits\":[{\"kind\":\"navigation_not_evid